content:
Owner: Devon Price (Release automation & internal tooling)
Last review: 2025-06-06 (Connor, Sahana)

Context
- The installer now generates a versioned “upgrade plan” artifact that can be:
  - printed for operator review (plan summary)
  - persisted to disk / support bundle (audit)
  - executed by the installer state machine (upgrade + rollback)
- This doc is a working schema draft for that artifact.

Primary goals (what the schema must support)
1) Deterministic execution ordering
   - stages -> steps with explicit dependencies and stable IDs
2) Clear failure modes
   - step-level on_failure behavior + where rollback can be invoked
3) Rollback entry points
   - explicit rollback hooks + constraints (e.g., schema migrations)
4) Auditability
   - include enough metadata to correlate to release artifacts + logs
5) Works for both VPC and on-prem/air-gapped
   - plan can reference either online artifact URLs or offline bundle paths + checksums

Non-goals (for v1)
- Representing arbitrarily complex multi-hop upgrades (N-3 -> N). v1 targets N-1 -> N.
- Encoding every internal migration detail. Plan references named operations; implementation defines mechanics.

Terminology
- Plan: top-level document produced by installer.
- Stage: a coarse phase (prechecks, backup, control-plane, data-plane, post-verify, finalize).
- Step: smallest unit of work the state machine can execute/record.
- Gate: a check that must pass to proceed (health, readiness, compatibility).

Versioning strategy
- plan_format_version: semver for the plan document itself (NOT the Redwood Private platform version)
- upgrade_target_version: the version of Redwood Private being installed/upgraded to
- upgrade_source_version: the version currently installed

Compatibility contract (draft)
- Installer must accept plan_format_version where major matches.
- Minor can add fields only (backward compatible additions).
- Patch can fix typos/constraints.

Top-level shape
- Plan is JSON (UTF-8)
- Must be stable for support bundles and offline execution
- Must not contain secrets
  - any secret material must be referenced (secret_ref) and resolved at runtime

JSON Schema draft (Draft-07)
NOTE: This is a draft. Field names and enums may still change.

{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://redwoodinference.com/schemas/private/upgrade-plan/v0.1.0.json",
  "title": "Redwood Private Upgrade Plan",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "plan_format_version",
    "plan_id",
    "generated_at",
    "generator",
    "upgrade",
    "environment",
    "artifacts",
    "stages"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "plan_format_version": { "type": "string", "description": "Semver for this plan format, e.g. 0.1.0" },
    "plan_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Stable identifier for plan; UUIDv4 preferred" },
    "generated_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },

    "generator": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["name", "version"],
      "properties": {
        "name": { "type": "string", "enum": ["redwood-private-installer"] },
        "version": { "type": "string", "description": "Installer build/version" },
        "git_sha": { "type": "string" },
        "build_date": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
      }
    },

    "upgrade": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["source_version", "target_version", "supported_path"],
      "properties": {
        "source_version": { "type": "string" },
        "target_version": { "type": "string" },
        "supported_path": { "type": "boolean", "description": "Result of compatibility policy evaluation" },
        "compatibility_report_ref": { "type": "string", "description": "Path/ref to a compatibility evaluation output (optional)" },
        "risk_level": { "type": "string", "enum": ["low", "medium", "high"] },
        "maintenance_window": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "start": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
            "end": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" },
            "timezone": { "type": "string", "description": "IANA tz name; best effort" }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "environment": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["mode", "cluster"],
      "properties": {
        "mode": { "type": "string", "enum": ["vpc", "onprem", "airgapped"] },
        "region": { "type": "string" },
        "customer_env_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Customer-provided environment identifier (optional)" },
        "cluster": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": ["kubernetes_version"],
          "properties": {
            "name": { "type": "string" },
            "kubernetes_version": { "type": "string" },
            "distribution": { "type": "string", "description": "e.g. eks, gke, aks, openshift, rke2" },
            "storage_backend": { "type": "string", "description": "e.g. ebs-csi, ceph, longhorn, nfs" }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "artifacts": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["manifest"],
      "properties": {
        "manifest": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": ["artifact_id", "type", "source"],
            "properties": {
              "artifact_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Stable ID used by steps" },
              "type": { "type": "string", "enum": ["helm_chart", "container_image", "bundle", "binary", "config"] },
              "source": {
                "type": "object",
                "additionalProperties": false,
                "required": ["mode"],
                "properties": {
                  "mode": { "type": "string", "enum": ["online", "offline"] },
                  "url": { "type": "string" },
                  "path": { "type": "string", "description": "Local filesystem path (offline bundle)" },
                  "sha256": { "type": "string" },
                  "signature_ref": { "type": "string", "description": "Optional signature file/ref" }
                }
              },
              "expected_version": { "type": "string" },
              "notes": { "type": "string" }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "stages": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["stage_id", "name", "kind", "steps"],
        "properties": {
          "stage_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Stable identifier (kebab-case preferred)" },
          "name": { "type": "string" },
          "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": ["precheck", "backup", "control_plane", "data_plane", "postcheck", "finalize"] },
          "depends_on": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "description": "List of stage_ids" },
          "operator_message": { "type": "string", "description": "Displayed at stage start (human readable)" },
          "rollback": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "allowed": { "type": "boolean" },
              "entrypoints": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "description": "step_ids that are safe rollback points" },
              "notes": { "type": "string" }
            }
          },
          "steps": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": ["step_id", "kind", "on_failure"],
              "properties": {
                "step_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Stable identifier (kebab-case preferred)" },
                "name": { "type": "string" },
                "kind": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "enum": [
                    "run_precheck",
                    "compute_plan",
                    "acquire_lock",
                    "backup_snapshot",
                    "backup_logical",
                    "helm_upgrade",
                    "db_migrate",
                    "restart_component",
                    "wait_for_ready",
                    "emit_audit_event",
                    "pause_for_operator",
                    "finalize_state"
                  ]
                },
                "component": { "type": "string", "description": "e.g. control-plane, api, scheduler, gateway, postgres" },
                "depends_on": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "description": "List of step_ids" },
                "inputs": { "type": "object", "description": "Free-form key/values; no secrets" },
                "artifact_refs": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "description": "List of artifact_id" },
                "timeout_seconds": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1 },
                "retries": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 0 },
                "health_gates": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "required": ["gate_id", "kind", "severity"],
                    "properties": {
                      "gate_id": { "type": "string" },
                      "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": ["k8s_ready", "http_ok", "db_ok", "disk_headroom", "oidc_reachable", "dns_ok"] },
                      "severity": { "type": "string", "enum": ["block", "warn"] },
                      "remediation": { "type": "string" }
                    }
                  }
                },
                "on_failure": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "required": ["action"],
                  "properties": {
                    "action": { "type": "string", "enum": ["abort", "pause", "attempt_rollback", "continue"] },
                    "rollback_to_step_id": { "type": "string", "description": "If attempt_rollback, preferred rollback target" },
                    "operator_hint": { "type": "string" }
                  }
                },
                "rollback_hooks": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "required": ["hook_id", "kind"],
                    "properties": {
                      "hook_id": { "type": "string" },
                      "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": ["pre_rollback", "rollback", "post_rollback"] },
                      "command_ref": { "type": "string", "description": "Named command within installer/runtime" },
                      "notes": { "type": "string" }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },

    "notes": { "type": "string" },

    "audit": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "correlation_id": { "type": "string", "description": "Used to link to audit log events" },
        "requested_by": { "type": "string", "description": "Operator identity (if provided)" },
        "change_ticket": { "type": "string", "description": "Optional: customer change ticket / internal ref" }
      }
    }
  }
}

Implementation notes (important constraints)
- Stable IDs
  - stage_id and step_id must not change across plan regeneration for the same source/target version unless semantics change.
  - reason: state machine persistence + support/debugging.

- Secrets
  - inputs MUST NOT contain secrets. If a step needs secret access, it should rely on runtime environment (K8s Secret) and only store a reference key.

- Offline bundles
  - artifact.source.mode=offline uses path + sha256 (and optional signature_ref).
  - Plan generation should include sha256 whenever possible to prevent “wrong bundle” execution.

- Operator UX
  - operator_message (stage) + operator_hint (on_failure) are intended to be shown in CLI.
  - Keep these short and actionable.

- Rollback
  - rollback.entrypoints should align with the rollback semantics doc (Confluence: rollback-semantics-and-hooks).
  - Not every stage is rollback-safe (e.g., after certain non-reversible migrations).

- Gates vs prechecks
  - “Prechecks” are usually a stage.
  - “Gates” can appear on steps (e.g., post-helm readiness) and can be warn/block.


Example payload (v0.1.0)
This is an illustrative plan for N-1 -> N in VPC mode.

{
  "plan_format_version": "0.1.0",
  "plan_id": "7a4d3c4e-19b1-4a57-91cf-7ce5c6d9a4c0",
  "generated_at": "2025-06-06T18:42:11Z",
  "generator": { "name": "redwood-private-installer", "version": "1.18.0", "git_sha": "c1f2a4b" },
  "upgrade": {
    "source_version": "private-2.31.0",
    "target_version": "private-2.32.0",
    "supported_path": true,
    "risk_level": "low",
    "maintenance_window": { "start": "2025-06-10T01:00:00Z", "end": "2025-06-10T03:00:00Z", "timezone": "UTC" }
  },
  "environment": {
    "mode": "vpc",
    "region": "us-east-1",
    "cluster": { "name": "redwood-private-prod", "kubernetes_version": "1.29", "distribution": "eks", "storage_backend": "ebs-csi" }
  },
  "artifacts": {
    "manifest": [
      {
        "artifact_id": "charts-redwood-private",
        "type": "helm_chart",
        "expected_version": "2.32.0",
        "source": { "mode": "online", "url": "https://charts.redwoodinference.com/private/redwood-private-2.32.0.tgz", "sha256": "<sha256>" },
        "notes": "Control plane + data plane charts (split phases)"
      },
      {
        "artifact_id": "image-control-plane",
        "type": "container_image",
        "expected_version": "2.32.0",
        "source": { "mode": "online", "url": "registry.redwoodinference.com/private/control-plane:2.32.0" }
      }
    ]
  },
  "audit": { "correlation_id": "upg-20250606-1842Z-7a4d", "requested_by": "ops@customer" },
  "stages": [
    {
      "stage_id": "prechecks",
      "name": "Preflight checks",
      "kind": "precheck",
      "operator_message": "Validating cluster health, storage, auth, DNS/TLS, and artifact reachability.",
      "rollback": { "allowed": false, "entrypoints": [], "notes": "No changes applied." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "prechecks-run",
          "name": "Run preflight suite",
          "kind": "run_precheck",
          "timeout_seconds": 900,
          "retries": 0,
          "health_gates": [
            { "gate_id": "disk-headroom", "kind": "disk_headroom", "severity": "block", "remediation": "Free 20%+ PV headroom or expand volumes; rerun prechecks." },
            { "gate_id": "oidc", "kind": "oidc_reachable", "severity": "warn", "remediation": "Verify IdP reachability from cluster egress; upgrades may fail at login flows." }
          ],
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort", "operator_hint": "Fix blocking prechecks and rerun 'installer upgrade plan' to regenerate." }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "backup",
      "name": "Backups",
      "kind": "backup",
      "depends_on": ["prechecks"],
      "operator_message": "Taking snapshots/backups required for rollback.",
      "rollback": { "allowed": true, "entrypoints": ["backup-complete"], "notes": "Rollback uses latest successful backup artifacts." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "backup-snapshot",
          "name": "Volume snapshot",
          "kind": "backup_snapshot",
          "component": "postgres",
          "timeout_seconds": 1800,
          "retries": 1,
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort", "operator_hint": "Snapshot failed. Do not proceed; verify CSI/EBS permissions and retry." }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "backup-complete",
          "name": "Record backup metadata",
          "kind": "finalize_state",
          "timeout_seconds": 60,
          "retries": 0,
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "control-plane",
      "name": "Control plane rollout",
      "kind": "control_plane",
      "depends_on": ["backup"],
      "operator_message": "Upgrading control plane components (API/console/orchestrator).",
      "rollback": { "allowed": true, "entrypoints": ["cp-helm-applied"], "notes": "Rollback permitted until irreversible migrations begin." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "cp-helm-apply",
          "name": "Apply control-plane Helm phase",
          "kind": "helm_upgrade",
          "artifact_refs": ["charts-redwood-private"],
          "inputs": { "phase": "control-plane" },
          "timeout_seconds": 1200,
          "retries": 0,
          "health_gates": [
            { "gate_id": "cp-ready", "kind": "k8s_ready", "severity": "block", "remediation": "Check pods/events; fix image pulls, node pressure, or RBAC issues." }
          ],
          "on_failure": { "action": "attempt_rollback", "rollback_to_step_id": "backup-complete", "operator_hint": "Control plane did not become ready. Attempting rollback to last known good." },
          "rollback_hooks": [
            { "hook_id": "cp-pre-rollback", "kind": "pre_rollback", "command_ref": "cordon-upgrade" },
            { "hook_id": "cp-rollback", "kind": "rollback", "command_ref": "helm-rollback-control-plane" },
            { "hook_id": "cp-post-rollback", "kind": "post_rollback", "command_ref": "verify-control-plane" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "step_id": "cp-helm-applied",
          "name": "Mark control-plane upgrade applied",
          "kind": "finalize_state",
          "timeout_seconds": 60,
          "retries": 0,
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "data-plane",
      "name": "Data plane rollout",
      "kind": "data_plane",
      "depends_on": ["control-plane"],
      "operator_message": "Upgrading data plane (workers, gateways) with readiness gates.",
      "rollback": { "allowed": true, "entrypoints": ["dp-helm-applied"], "notes": "Rollback may require draining or cache invalidation." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "dp-helm-apply",
          "name": "Apply data-plane Helm phase",
          "kind": "helm_upgrade",
          "artifact_refs": ["charts-redwood-private"],
          "inputs": { "phase": "data-plane" },
          "timeout_seconds": 1800,
          "retries": 0,
          "health_gates": [
            { "gate_id": "dp-ready", "kind": "k8s_ready", "severity": "block", "remediation": "Investigate gateway/worker readiness and node capacity; consider scaling." }
          ],
          "on_failure": { "action": "pause", "operator_hint": "Data plane failed readiness. Inspect pods and events; choose to continue or rollback." }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "dp-helm-applied",
          "name": "Mark data-plane upgrade applied",
          "kind": "finalize_state",
          "timeout_seconds": 60,
          "retries": 0,
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "postchecks",
      "name": "Post-upgrade verification",
      "kind": "postcheck",
      "depends_on": ["data-plane"],
      "operator_message": "Verifying control-plane connectivity, DB health, and request success rate.",
      "rollback": { "allowed": true, "entrypoints": ["verify-complete"], "notes": "Rollback still possible if verification fails and migrations are reversible." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "verify-ready",
          "name": "Wait for system healthy",
          "kind": "wait_for_ready",
          "timeout_seconds": 900,
          "retries": 0,
          "health_gates": [
            { "gate_id": "http-ok", "kind": "http_ok", "severity": "block", "remediation": "Check ingress/gateway, certs, DNS, and control plane logs." },
            { "gate_id": "db-ok", "kind": "db_ok", "severity": "block", "remediation": "Check DB connections, migrations status, and lock contention." }
          ],
          "on_failure": { "action": "attempt_rollback", "rollback_to_step_id": "backup-complete", "operator_hint": "Verification failed. Rolling back to pre-upgrade snapshot." }
        },
        {
          "step_id": "verify-complete",
          "name": "Record verification success",
          "kind": "finalize_state",
          "timeout_seconds": 60,
          "retries": 0,
          "on_failure": { "action": "abort" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "finalize",
      "name": "Finalize",
      "kind": "finalize",
      "depends_on": ["postchecks"],
      "operator_message": "Finalizing upgrade state and emitting audit events.",
      "rollback": { "allowed": false, "entrypoints": [], "notes": "After finalize, rollback requires explicit operator procedure." },
      "steps": [
        {
          "step_id": "audit-upgrade-complete",
          "name": "Emit audit event",
          "kind": "emit_audit_event",
          "timeout_seconds": 30,
          "retries": 3,
          "inputs": { "event": "private_upgrade_complete" },
          "on_failure": { "action": "continue", "operator_hint": "Audit emission failed; upgrade considered successful but investigate SIEM/audit pipeline." }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Generated as part of Private upgrade plan v1. Control-plane/data-plane phases assume helm chart split (PR-2204)."
}

Open questions / TODOs
1) inputs type
   - For now: free-form object (no secrets). Do we want to constrain inputs per kind in v0.2.0?
2) rollback_to_step_id
   - Should this be validated to a declared rollback entrypoint only?
3) artifact manifest
   - Do we need a first-class "oci_ref" field (vs url) for charts/images?
4) plan signing
   - For regulated on-prem: should the plan itself be signed (separate from bundle signature)?
5) schema migrations
   - Need a way to flag an irreversible migration so the plan can mark rollback.allowed=false after that step.
   - Possible addition: step.outputs: { "rollback_safe": false }

Changelog
- 2025-05-07: Initial skeleton (stages/steps + artifacts)
- 2025-05-21: Added rollback entrypoints and on_failure semantics
- 2025-06-06: Added audit/correlation_id and offline artifact source fields
